1. PRODUCT
========================================
Most typing tests use prose. Developers type symbols, flags and commands ({ } [ ] ( ) => !== && || | ~ $ @ # \ / --) and nobody trains them. Backspace is typing practice for the characters developers actually type: git, terminal, Docker, SQL, code and AI prompts, plus a symbol-drill mode, per-key analytics that find your slowest and most error-prone keys, and adaptive practice built from them. Everything runs in the browser and works offline. No account in v1. All data stays on the device.
