6. TYPING ENGINE AND LOGIC (plain TypeScript, no React)
========================================
Input: capture "keydown" on a hidden input or focused container. Use event.key, ignore modifier-only keys, handle IME composition safely, block paste, cut and drag. Timestamp every keystroke with performance.now(). React renders from engine state, but the whole text must NOT re-render on each key: render lines as memoised components and update only the active line's character spans (or use refs), so input latency is imperceptible. Animate only transform and opacity.
Per-test state: target lines, typed buffer per line, caret position, keystroke log [{t, expected, typed, correct}], per-second samples, start and end timestamps, mode config.
Metrics:
- correctChars: characters in committed and current lines that match the target (a correctly completed line's Enter counts as 1).
- netWPM = (correctChars / 5) / minutes. rawWPM = (all typed characters / 5) / minutes. Minutes = elapsed time since the first keystroke.
- accuracy% = correct keystrokes / total keystrokes x 100 (corrected mistakes still count as errors).
- consistency% = 100 minus the coefficient of variation of per-second WPM, clamped 0-100.
- backspaceScore = round(netWPM x (accuracy/100)^2). Use it as the headline score for personal bests alongside WPM.
Per-key stats (persisted): for each expected character keep count, totalLatencyMs (time since the previous keystroke; ignore gaps over 2000 ms) and errors. Also keep bigram stats (previous character + expected character) for a future version.
Slow keys: keys with at least 8 samples, ranked by average latency. Error keys: ranked by error rate, minimum 8 samples. Show the top N.
ADAPTIVE "My weak keys" mode: score each line in all banks as the sum of per-character weights (normalised slowness + error rate), pick high-scoring lines, shuffle, and mix in 20% general lines so it is not repetitive.
Streaks: a day counts if at least one test of 30 seconds or longer was completed, evaluated in the local time zone. Compute current and longest streak.
XP and levels: XP per completed test = round(backspaceScore / 2) + 10. Level = floor(sqrt(XP / 50)) + 1. Titles: levels 1-2 Intern, 3-4 Junior, 5-7 Mid, 8-11 Senior, 12-17 Staff, 18+ Principal. Show a level-up modal when a threshold is crossed.
Badges (data-driven): First Test; 10 Tests; 100 Tests; 7-Day Streak; 30-Day Streak; 50 WPM (95%+ accuracy); 80 WPM (95%+ accuracy); Flawless (100% accuracy, 30s or longer); Symbol Slayer (Symbols, 40+ WPM, 95%+ accuracy); Marathoner (finish a 300s test); Night Owl (a test completed between 00:00 and 04:00 local time).
A test is saved only if at least 5 seconds were typed and at least 10 characters. Tests cancelled with Esc are not saved.
Stored objects: settings, results[] (cap 500, newest first), keyStats, bigramStats, streak dates, xp, badges, personalBests keyed by "category|time|level", onboarding flags.

